The machine-readable authority is `security/exception-register.yml`. This page explains its present entries.

| ID | Gap | Mitigation | Expiry |
|---|---|---|---|
| SEC-GOV-001 | No independent human reviewer in the solo operation | deterministic gates plus explicit owner approval; no two-person claim | 2026-10-27 |
| SEC-CSP-001 | preserved Phase 1 markup needs inline style and handler exceptions | scripts remain origin-restricted; objects and framing are denied | 2026-10-27 |
| SEC-RATE-001 | no durable distributed contact rate limit configured | Turnstile, request cap, allowlists, honeypot, and duplicate damping | 2026-08-27 |
| SEC-DEP-001 | Excalidraw Animate development tree carries one high and nine moderate transitive advisories | production audit is clear; trusted scenes only; scheduled full audit stays visible | 2026-08-26 |

Exceptions do not turn a missing control into an implemented control. Owners review them before expiry and either remove the gap, replace the exception with fresh evidence, or stop the affected release.
